Graph: Model

Purpose:
  Define the formal data model for .sdd entities and relationships.
  This is the semantic layer that maps .sdd files to a queryable
  knowledge graph. Files are storage; entities are identity;
  relationships are meaning.

Owns: ./

Scope:
  Entity definition and lifecycle
  Relationship types and metadata
  Node and edge typing
  Cardinality rules
  Identity vs version separation
  Hybrid storage model (filesystem + PostgreSQL + graph)
  Temporal graph and snapshots
  Graph schema constraints

Principles:
  Entity ≠ File. File is representation; entity is identity.
  Relationships use IDs, not text names.
  Graph is logical model; storage is physical concern.
  History is immutable — entities and relationships are versioned.
  Schema constraints are machine-checkable.

Entity:
  structure:
    id: string (immutable, e.g. TASK-100, REQ-001)
    type: string (Task, Requirement, Skill, Agent, Policy, Decision, Artifact, Domain, Entity, API, Table, Test, Execution, Event)
    version: string (semver: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH)
    status: string (DRAFT, ACTIVE, DEPRECATED, ARCHIVED)
    created_at: timestamp
    updated_at: timestamp

  lifecycle:
    DRAFT -> ACTIVE -> DEPRECATED -> ARCHIVED

  identity:
    rule: ID never changes
    rule: version changes do not change identity
    rule: TASK-100 v1, v2, v3 are the same entity

Relationship:
  structure:
    from_id: string
    relation: string (implements, requires, assigned_to, depends_on, produces, verifies, affects, governed_by, supersedes, exposes, owns, uses, executes, emitted_by, belongs_to)
    to_id: string
    metadata: object
    version: string

  types:
    implements: Requirement -> Task
    requires: Task -> Skill
    assigned_to: Task -> Agent
    depends_on: Task -> Task
    produces: Task -> Artifact
    verifies: Test -> Requirement
    affects: Decision -> Domain | API | Task
    governed_by: Task -> Policy
    supersedes: Decision -> Decision
    exposes: Domain -> API
    owns: Domain -> Entity | Table
    uses: Execution -> Plan
    executes: Execution -> Task
    emitted_by: Event -> Agent
    belongs_to: Event -> Execution

  metadata:
    reason: string
    blocking: boolean
    mandatory: boolean
    environment: string

GraphSchema:
  node_types:
    - Requirement
    - Feature
    - Domain
    - Entity
    - API
    - Table
    - Task
    - Skill
    - Agent
    - Workflow
    - Policy
    - Decision
    - Test
    - Artifact
    - Execution
    - Event

  edge_types:
    - implements
    - requires
    - assigned_to
    - depends_on
    - produces
    - verifies
    - affects
    - governed_by
    - supersedes
    - exposes
    - owns
    - uses
    - executes
    - emitted_by
    - belongs_to

  cardinality:
    Task -> assigned_to -> Agent: 1..1
    Task -> requires -> Skill: 0..N
    Task -> depends_on -> Task: 0..N
    Requirement -> implemented_by -> Task: 0..N

StorageModel:
  filesystem:
    purpose: human navigation and git-friendly editing
    rule: folders are navigation, not domain model
    rule: .sdd files are entity representations

  postgresql:
    purpose: transactions, versioning, audit, constraints, structured queries
    tables:
      - entities (id, type, version, status, data JSONB)
      - relationships (from_id, relation, to_id, metadata JSONB, version)
      - events (id, type, data JSONB, timestamp)
      - executions (id, plan_version, state)

  graph_abstraction:
    purpose: semantic queries, impact analysis, traversal
    rule: graph is logical layer over PostgreSQL
    rule: physical storage and domain model are decoupled

TemporalGraph:
  rule: relationship changes are versioned
  rule: historical queries MUST be supported
  rule: graph snapshots MUST be created for executions

  example:
    2026-08-01: TASK-100 depends_on TASK-90
    2026-08-10: TASK-100 depends_on TASK-95

  query: "What was the dependency on August 5?"

Snapshot:
  rule: execution creates graph snapshot
  rule: snapshot is immutable
  rule: snapshot ID is recorded in execution record

Security:
  rule: graph relationships are permission-aware
  rule: agents see only authorized subgraphs
  rule: SECURITY_POLICY and SECRETS nodes are never exposed to low-trust agents

GraphIntegrity:
  rule: impossible relationships MUST be detected
  rule: typed edge rules MUST be enforced
  rule: orphan nodes MUST be flagged (unless intentional: tech debt, research)

Navigation:
  Graph: @graph/INDEX.sdd
  Nodes: @graph/nodes.sdd
  Relations: @graph/relations.sdd
  Traceability: @graph/traceability.sdd
  Impact: @graph/impact.sdd
  Ownership: @graph/ownership.sdd
  Dependencies: @graph/dependencies.sdd
  Coverage: @graph/coverage.sdd
  Drift: @graph/drift.sdd
  Data: @../architecture/data.sdd

Rules:
  [GR-MODEL-01] Every entity MUST have immutable ID.
  [GR-MODEL-02] Relationships MUST reference IDs, not text names.
  [GR-MODEL-03] Entity identity is separate from version.
  [GR-MODEL-04] Graph stores relationships, not file copies.
  [GR-MODEL-05] Relationship types MUST have explicit source and target node types.
  [GR-MODEL-06] Cardinality rules MUST be enforced.
  [GR-MODEL-07] Relationship changes MUST be versioned.
  [GR-MODEL-08] Graph snapshots MUST be created for reproducibility.
  [GR-MODEL-09] Permission boundaries MUST be enforced on graph traversal.
  [GR-MODEL-10] Orphan nodes MUST be explicitly allowed or flagged.

State: +
